    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d67">

                <pb facs="0159" n="69" xml:id="pg69"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.73/23: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-12-14T11:00:00-05:29"><hi rendition="#italic">December 14,
                                1920—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 8:44
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>346. Dr. de Bustamante<anchor n="74" xml:id="d67-f1"/> informs me that President
                    Menocal is greatly interested in the matter of the Western Union Telegraph
                    Company, and he believes that if the Government of the United States should
                    request the suspension of the concession President Menocal would act
                    immediately.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Long</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d67-f1" n="74" xml:id="d67-f1-content">
                <p>Attorney in Habana for the All America Cables, Incorporated.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
